{"path":"types/is_within_lifetime","title":"std::is_within_lifetime","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>is_within_lifetime","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/is_within_lifetime","section":"types","kind":"page","summary":"Determines whether the pointer ptr points to an object that is within its lifetime.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/type_traits\">&lt;type_traits&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx26\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>consteval <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> is_within_lifetime<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> T<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> ptr <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx26\">(since C++26)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Determines whether the pointer <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">ptr</span></code> points to an object that is within its <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/lifetime\">lifetime</a>.\n</p><p>During the evaluation of an expression <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">E</span></code> as a core constant expression, a call to <code>std::is_within_lifetime</code> is ill-formed unless <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">ptr</span></code> points to an object\n</p>\n<ul><li> that is <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/constant_expression#Usable_in_constant_expressions\">usable in constant expressions</a>, or\n</li><li> whose complete object’s lifetime began within <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">E</span></code>.\n</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> p\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> pointer to detect\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code> if pointer <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">ptr</span></code> points to an object that is within its lifetime; otherwise <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<table class=\"wikitable ftm-begin ftm-has-value\">\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/feature_test\">Feature-test</a> macro</th>\n<th><abbr>Value</abbr></th>\n<th><abbr>Std</abbr></th>\n<th>Feature\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/feature_test#cpp_lib_is_within_lifetime\"><code>__cpp_lib_is_within_lifetime</code></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/compiler_support/26#cpp_lib_is_within_lifetime_202306L\"><code>202306L</code></a></td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark\">(C++26)</span></td>\n<td>Checking if a union alternative is active\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\"><p><code>std::is_within_lifetime</code> can be used to check whether a union member is active:</p>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;type_traits&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"co1\">// an optional boolean type occupying only one byte,</span>\n<span class=\"co1\">// assuming sizeof(bool) == sizeof(char)</span>\n<span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> optional_bool\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">union</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span> <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> b<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> c<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// assuming the value representations for true and false</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// are distinct from the value representation for 2</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> optional_bool<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> c<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> optional_bool<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> b<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> b<span class=\"br0\">(</span>b<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> has_value<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"kw1\">if</span> consteval\n        <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n            <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">is_within_lifetime</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>b<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// during constant evaluation,</span>\n                                                <span class=\"co1\">// cannot read from c</span>\n        <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n        <span class=\"kw1\">else</span>\n        <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n            <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> c <span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// during runtime, must read from c</span>\n        <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> operator<span class=\"sy2\">*</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> b<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> optional_bool disengaged<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> optional_bool engaged<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw2\">true</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    static_assert<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">!</span>disengaged.<span class=\"me1\">has_value</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    static_assert<span class=\"br0\">(</span>engaged.<span class=\"me1\">has_value</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    static_assert<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>engaged<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n</div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"types","title":"Type support (basic types, RTTI)"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::is_within_lifetime","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++26. Determines whether the pointer ptr points to an object that is within its lifetime."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"p"},{"label":"Return value","note":"true if pointer ptr points to an object that is within its lifetime; otherwise false."},{"label":"Notes"},{"label":"Example","note":"std::is_within_lifetime can be used to check whether a union member is active:"}]},"standards":["C++26"],"wordCount":236,"codeBlockCount":1}
